@@ -0,0 +1,78 @@
+# Native codegen feature boundary
+
+Status: Experimental implementation boundary.
+
+The embedded mobile runtime must be buildable without runtime executable-code
+generation and without linking Cranelift.
+
+## Cargo profiles
+
+Default/full runtime:
+
+```sh
+cargo build
+```
+
+continues to enable `native-codegen`.
+
+Interpreter-only mobile library:
+
+```sh
+cargo check --lib --no-default-features --features mobile-runtime
+```
+
+`mobile-runtime` is deliberately an empty marker feature. The bytecode VM,
+actors, frozen `.nbc` loader, C embedding ABI, and pre-registered FFI callbacks
+are part of the base library.
+
+Dynamic native library loading remains a separate `ffi` feature. The mobile UI
+bridge does not require it because callbacks are registered in-process.
+
+## `native-codegen`
+
+The feature owns both:
+
+- tiered Cranelift JIT;
+- the current AOT backend.
+
+The current AOT implementation uses `cranelift_jit::JITModule`, so calling it
+"AOT" does not make it safe to include in an iOS runtime binary. Both code paths
+therefore stay behind the same feature until true object-file AOT is separated.
+
+Cranelift crates and `target-lexicon` are optional dependencies activated only
+by `native-codegen`.
+
+## Stable VM boundary
+
+`JitBackend` remains always compiled. When `native-codegen` is absent,
+`create_default_jit()` returns `None`, so VM construction naturally stays on
+the bytecode interpreter without conditional code in the VM data model.
+
+Actor JIT scheduling counters also remain in the actor layout for now; the
+neutral safepoint constant lives in `backends`. Concrete AOT targets/module
+storage and JIT thread-local wiring are compiled only with `native-codegen`.
+
+## WASM
+
+For this first split, `wasm-backend` implies `native-